# Web News Aggregation & Visualization — Backend Documentation

**Team role covered by this document:** Backend & Database
**Stack:** Node.js, Express 5, MongoDB, Mongoose 9, JWT, Joi, node-cron, NewsAPI

---

## 1. Folder Structure

```
backend/
├── config/           # db.js — MongoDB connection
├── constants/        # newsCategoryMap.js, countryCoordinates.js (if geo-fencing added)
├── controllers/       # Thin request/response handlers, one per resource
├── docs/              # This file and related API references
├── helpers/           # (reserved — currently unused)
├── jobs/              # node-cron scheduled tasks
├── middleware/         # asyncHandler, errorHandler, authMiddleware
├── models/            # Mongoose schemas
├── repositories/       # ONLY layer allowed to query MongoDB directly
├── routes/            # Express routers, mapped to controllers
├── seed/              # One-time idempotent data seed scripts
├── services/          # Business logic, sits between controllers and repositories
├── tests/             # Reserved for automated tests (currently empty — gap, see audit)
├── utils/             # AppError, generateToken, slugify, dateHelpers, chartHelpers
├── validators/         # Joi schemas + validation middleware
├── app.js             # Express app, middleware pipeline, route mounting
└── server.js          # Entry point — env config, DB connect, cron start, listen
```

**Architectural rule enforced throughout:** routes → controllers (thin) → services (business logic) → repositories (the only DB access layer) → models (schema).

