## 9. Controllers

One controller file per resource (`authController`, `categoryController`, `sourceController`, `articleController`, `newsIngestionController`, `dashboardController`, `trendingController`, `visualizationController`, `bookmarkController`, `readingHistoryController`, `commentController`). Every controller is intentionally thin: receive request → call one service function → shape the HTTP response. No validation, no business rules, no direct DB access ever lives here.

---

## 10. Services

Business logic layer — duplicate checks, ownership checks, orchestration across multiple repositories (e.g. `articleService.searchArticles` combines category resolution, source resolution, and the actual search+count queries). Services are the only layer allowed to `throw new AppError(...)`.

