## 12. Middleware

- `asyncHandler` — wraps async controllers so thrown errors/rejected promises are forwarded to `errorHandler` automatically, eliminating repetitive try/catch.
- `errorHandler` — centralized, 4-argument error middleware; translates Mongoose CastErrors, duplicate-key errors, ValidationErrors, and JWT errors into consistent HTTP status codes + messages.
- `authMiddleware` — `protect`, `authorize`, `attachUserIfPresent` (see Section 7).

---

## 13. Utilities

`AppError` (custom error class carrying a statusCode), `generateToken` (JWT signing), `slugify` (category slug generation), `dateHelpers` (startOfToday/daysAgo), `chartHelpers` (toChartFormat/fillDateGaps).

---

## 14. External APIs

**NewsAPI** (`newsapi.org/v2/top-headlines`) — fetched per-category on a cron schedule. Category mapping note: NewsAPI has no "politics" category; our "Politics" category is mapped to NewsAPI's `general` category as the closest available match.

